# promise: #641
# A Little Window behind another app's window (`cover`, as Slack in the report) comes to the front when it is
# clicked, as in Arc. It is a non-activating panel: macOS let the click through without letting Cra come
# forward, and the window stayed behind the other app (GitHub #641).
budget rss=900 stalls50=40
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "defaultLinkDestination": {"littleWindow": {}}}
pace 0.5

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=main
wait 2
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
cover
cra://debug?yieldTo=${COVER}
wait 1
cover link
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=little
wait 2
# The other app comes back over it.
cra://debug?yieldTo=${COVER}
wait 1.5
cra://debug?littleFocus=covered
expect-log little focus covered: active=0 key=none over=[1-9] windows=1
cra://debug?clickAt=200,120&target=little
wait 1.5
cra://debug?littleFocus=clicked
expect-log little focus clicked: active=\d key=\S+ over=0 windows=1
